<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
    <template id="documentation_page" name="Resend Email Connector - Documentation">
        <t t-call="web.layout">
            <t t-set="title">Resend Email Connector - Documentation</t>
            <div class="container py-4" id="resend_documentation">
                <style>
                    #resend_documentation { max-width: 980px; }
                    #resend_documentation h1 { font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
                    #resend_documentation h2 { margin-top: 36px; font-size: 22px; font-weight: 600; }
                    #resend_documentation h3 { margin-top: 22px; font-size: 17px; font-weight: 600; }
                    #resend_documentation p, #resend_documentation li { line-height: 1.6; }
                    #resend_documentation code { background: #f3f3f7; padding: 1px 5px; border-radius: 3px; }
                    #resend_documentation pre { background: #14141a; color: #f2f2f5; padding: 14px; border-radius: 6px; overflow-x: auto; }
                    #resend_documentation .step { border-left: 3px solid #14141a; padding-left: 16px; margin: 18px 0; }
                    #resend_documentation .step > h3 { margin-top: 0; }
                    #resend_documentation table { font-size: 14px; }
                    #resend_documentation .toc a { display: block; padding: 2px 0; }
                </style>

                <div class="d-flex justify-content-between align-items-start mb-3">
                    <div>
                        <h1 class="mb-1">Resend Email Connector</h1>
                        <p class="text-muted mb-0">
                            Setup guide for administrators and users. Sends and receives Odoo
                            email through Resend and keeps the delivery status of each message.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <a class="btn btn-outline-dark" href="/web#action=resend_connector.action_resend_settings">
                        Open settings
                    </a>
                </div>

                <div t-if="not is_admin" class="alert alert-warning">
                    Only administrators can change this configuration. The page can be read
                    by every user.
                </div>

                <div class="alert alert-secondary" role="status">
                    <b>Current status.</b>
                    <span t-if="config['enabled'] and config['api_key']">Resend is enabled.</span>
                    <span t-if="not config['enabled']">The master switch is off, email goes through SMTP.</span>
                    <span t-if="config['enabled'] and not config['api_key']">The master switch is on but no API key is set.</span>
                    <br/>
                    <b>Webhook URL:</b> <code t-out="webhook_url"/>
                </div>

                <div class="row">
                    <div class="col-lg-7">
                        <h2 id="about">1. What the module does</h2>
                        <p>
                            Odoo prepares email as usual: templates, quotations, invoices, chatter
                            notifications, mass mailings, attachments, Bcc and alias domains. The
                            module replaces only the transport. Instead of opening an SMTP
                            connection, the message is sent to the Resend API over HTTPS, and the
                            events Resend reports are written back to the Odoo record.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            Incoming mail can be received from Resend as well. The module downloads
                            the original message, restores the reference to the Odoo thread and
                            passes it to Odoo's mail gateway, so replies appear in the chatter.
                        </p>

                        <h2 id="before">2. Before you start</h2>
                        <ul>
                            <li>You can log in to Odoo as an administrator.</li>
                            <li>You have access to the DNS records of the sending domain.</li>
                            <li>Odoo has a public HTTPS address. It is required for delivery webhooks.</li>
                            <li>You have a Resend account (a free plan is enough for testing).</li>
                        </ul>

                        <h2 id="key">3. Create a Resend account and API key</h2>
                        <div class="step">
                            <ol>
                                <li>Create an account on <a href="https://resend.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">resend.com</a>.</li>
                                <li>Open API Keys and create a key.
                                    <ul>
                                        <li><b>Full access</b> is needed to manage domains and webhooks from Odoo.</li>
                                        <li><b>Sending access</b> is enough if domains and webhooks are configured in the Resend dashboard.</li>
                                    </ul>
                                </li>
                                <li>Copy the key, it starts with <code>re_</code>, and paste it in the settings.</li>
                            </ol>
                        </div>

                        <h2 id="domain">4. Verify a sending domain</h2>
                        <div class="step">
                            <ol>
                                <li>Open <b>Resend &gt; Domains</b>, create the domain and click
                                    <b>Register in Resend</b>.</li>
                                <li>Copy the SPF and DKIM records shown on the form to your DNS provider.</li>
                                <li>Add a DMARC record, for example
                                    <code>v=DMARC1; p=none; rua=mailto:dmarc@example.com</code>.</li>
                                <li>Click <b>Verify Now</b> and wait for DNS propagation.</li>
                            </ol>
                            <p class="text-muted mb-0">
                                A subdomain such as mg.example.com is recommended, so the reputation
                                of the email domain is independent from the main website.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                        <div t-if="domains" class="table-responsive">
                            <table class="table table-sm">
                                <thead>
                                    <tr><th>Domain</th><th>Status</th><th>Records</th></tr>
                                </thead>
                                <tbody>
                                    <tr t-foreach="domains" t-as="domain">
                                        <td><t t-out="domain.name"/></td>
                                        <td>
                                            <span class="badge"
                                                t-attf-class="badge #{'text-bg-success' if domain.status == 'verified' else 'text-bg-warning'}">
                                                <t t-out="domain.status"/>
                                            </span>
                                        </td>
                                        <td>
                                            <div t-foreach="domain.record_ids" t-as="record" class="small">
                                                <b t-out="record.record_type"/> <t t-out="record.name"/>
                                                = <code t-out="record.value"/>
                                            </div>
                                        </td>
                                    </tr>
                                </tbody>
                            </table>
                        </div>

                        <h2 id="configure">5. Configure outgoing email</h2>
                        <div class="step">
                            <ol>
                                <li>In <b>Settings &gt; Discuss &gt; Resend</b> tick
                                    <b>Send emails through Resend</b>, paste the API key and set the
                                    <b>From Address</b> on the verified domain.</li>
                                <li>Leave <b>Rewrite From</b> on its default value. Odoo may choose a
                                    sender on a domain Resend does not know; the module then sends
                                    from the verified address and keeps the original sender in
                                    Reply-To.</li>
                                <li>Open <b>Settings &gt; Technical &gt; Outgoing Mail Servers</b>,
                                    tick <b>Use Resend API</b> on the server Odoo should use and click
                                    <b>Test Connection</b>.</li>
                            </ol>
                            <p class="text-muted mb-0">
                                Servers without the option keep using SMTP. The master switch is a
                                quick way to disable Resend for all servers.
                            </p>
                        </div>

                        <h2 id="test">6. Send a test email</h2>
                        <div class="step">
                            <p>
                                Open a quotation or an invoice and send it by email, then open
                                <b>Resend &gt; Emails</b>. The row shows the Resend id and the
                                status. The test wizard in the settings sends a message through the
                                full pipeline.
                            </p>
                            <p class="mb-1">Without a verified domain, Resend accepts only these recipients:</p>
                            <ul>
                                <li><code>delivered@resend.dev</code>: delivered;</li>
                                <li><code>bounced@resend.dev</code>: hard bounce;</li>
                                <li><code>complained@resend.dev</code>: delivered, then marked as spam;</li>
                                <li><code>suppressed@resend.dev</code>: suppressed address.</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>

                        <h2 id="webhook">7. Delivery webhooks</h2>
                        <div class="step">
                            <ol>
                                <li>Check the <b>Webhook URL</b> in the settings. Odoo must be
                                    reachable from the internet at that address. If required, set
                                    <b>Public Base URL</b> to the public address of the instance.</li>
                                <li>Click <b>Create / update webhook in Resend</b>. The endpoint is
                                    created, subscribed to the email events and the signing secret is
                                    stored.</li>
                                <li>Open <b>Resend &gt; Configuration &gt; Webhook Events</b> to see
                                    the calls received from Resend.</li>
                            </ol>
                            <p class="mb-1">Events used by the module:</p>
                            <pre>email.sent, email.delivered, email.delivery_delayed, email.opened,
email.clicked, email.bounced, email.complained, email.failed,
email.suppressed, email.received</pre>
                            <p class="text-muted mb-0">
                                Every call is verified with the Svix HMAC-SHA256 signature, a five
                                minute tolerance and a unique event id. Calls that cannot be
                                processed immediately are retried by a scheduled job.
                            </p>
                        </div>

                        <h2 id="inbound">8. Receive incoming email</h2>
                        <div class="step">
                            <ol>
                                <li>Add the MX record of a subdomain, for example reply.example.com,
                                    to your DNS provider. Resend uses the record with the lowest
                                    priority.</li>
                                <li>Set <b>Settings &gt; Discuss &gt; Alias Domain</b> to that
                                    subdomain.</li>
                                <li>Create a <b>mail.alias</b> for the address, for example
                                    sales@reply.example.com, or simply reply to an email sent from
                                    Odoo.</li>
                            </ol>
                            <p class="text-muted mb-0">
                                Every address on the receiving domain is accepted by Resend.
                                Routing is done by Odoo. Messages without a matching alias are
                                listed in <b>Resend &gt; Inbound</b> with the status No Route.
                            </p>
                        </div>

                        <h2 id="status">9. Delivery statuses</h2>
                        <div class="table-responsive">
                            <table class="table table-sm">
                                <thead><tr><th>Status</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Odoo</th></tr></thead>
                                <tbody>
                                    <tr><td>Sent</td><td>Accepted by the Resend API</td><td>Email sent</td></tr>
                                    <tr><td>Delivered</td><td>Accepted by the recipient server</td><td>Notification delivered</td></tr>
                                    <tr><td>Delivery delayed</td><td>Resend is still retrying</td><td>Warning only</td></tr>
                                    <tr><td>Opened / Clicked</td><td>Tracking events</td><td>Informational</td></tr>
                                    <tr><td>Bounced</td><td>Rejected by the recipient server</td><td>Email failed, notification bounced</td></tr>
                                    <tr><td>Complained</td><td>Marked as spam by the recipient</td><td>Notification cancelled</td></tr>
                                    <tr><td>Failed</td><td>Quota, invalid data, blocked attachment</td><td>Email failed with the reason</td></tr>
                                </tbody>
                            </table>
                        </div>

                        <h2 id="troubleshooting">10. Troubleshooting</h2>
                        <div class="accordion" id="resendFaq">
                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <h2 class="accordion-header"><button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq1">The email is not sent</button></h2>
                                <div id="faq1" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#resendFaq">
                                    <div class="accordion-body">
                                        Open the email and read the failure reason. It contains the
                                        Resend error, for example domain is not verified,
                                        invalid_api_key or daily_quota_exceeded.
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <h2 class="accordion-header"><button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq2">No delivery status appears</button></h2>
                                <div id="faq2" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#resendFaq">
                                    <div class="accordion-body">
                                        Open Resend &gt; Configuration &gt; Webhook Events. If the
                                        list is empty, the webhook is missing or Odoo is not
                                        reachable from the internet.
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <h2 class="accordion-header"><button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq3">The webhook answers 401</button></h2>
                                <div id="faq3" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#resendFaq">
                                    <div class="accordion-body">
                                        The signing secret does not match. Copy the secret from the
                                        Resend dashboard again and check the server clock.
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <h2 class="accordion-header"><button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq4">Replies do not appear in the chatter</button></h2>
                                <div id="faq4" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#resendFaq">
                                    <div class="accordion-body">
                                        Check the MX record, the email.received subscription, the
                                        Alias Domain and the Inbound list for messages without a
                                        route.
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <h2 class="accordion-header"><button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq5">Mass mailing is slow</button></h2>
                                <div id="faq5" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#resendFaq">
                                    <div class="accordion-body">
                                        Resend allows 10 requests per second per team. The module
                                        limits itself to 8 and retries the rest, so the mailing takes
                                        longer but no message is lost.
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <h2 id="security">11. Security</h2>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Webhook calls are verified with the Svix signature, a constant time
                                comparison and a five minute tolerance. Duplicate calls are ignored.</li>
                            <li>The API key and the signing secret are system parameters that only
                                administrators can read. They are never written to the log.</li>
                            <li>Each email is sent with an idempotency key, so a retry cannot deliver
                                it twice.</li>
                            <li>Attachments are checked against the file types and the size allowed
                                by Resend before sending.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>

                    <div class="col-lg-5">
                        <div class="border rounded p-3 toc">
                            <b>Contents</b>
                            <a href="#about">1. What the module does</a>
                            <a href="#before">2. Before you start</a>
                            <a href="#key">3. Account and API key</a>
                            <a href="#domain">4. Verify a domain</a>
                            <a href="#configure">5. Configure outgoing email</a>
                            <a href="#test">6. Send a test email</a>
                            <a href="#webhook">7. Delivery webhooks</a>
                            <a href="#inbound">8. Incoming email</a>
                            <a href="#status">9. Delivery statuses</a>
                            <a href="#troubleshooting">10. Troubleshooting</a>
                            <a href="#security">11. Security</a>
                        </div>
                        <div class="alert alert-info mt-3 small">
                            The complete guide, including DNS details and a Russian version, is
                            shipped in the <b>doc</b> folder of the module.
                        </div>
                        <div class="border rounded p-3 mt-3 small text-muted">
                            <b>Resend Email Connector 1.0.0</b><br/>
                            POLISHCHUK &amp; SONS LTD<br/>
                            <a href="https://rex.cy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://rex.cy</a><br/>
                            License LGPL-3.0
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </t>
    </template>
</odoo>
